    },
    "body": "Instead of computing the values lazily (which doesn't play well with Ractors), this now computes the values when the schema is loaded. Now, as long as the schema is loaded on the main Ractor, these values can be used on non-main Ractors.\r\n\r\nFor some code specific \"why\":\r\n- Hooking reload_from_schema_cache is no longer needed because when the\r\n  schema reloads, the SchemaContext object is thrown away (so there's\r\n  nothing to manually reset)\r\n- timestamp_attribute_for_{create,update} were made public because we\r\n  have to call them inside the SchemaContext now",
    "created_at": "2026-09-10T23:18:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-11T16:12:12Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-11T05:28:42Z",
